Subject: [PATCH] tests: arith lifted by Remill and compiled to x86_64 matches
 an Unicorn AArch64 reference

arm64_ref.py runs a fixture function on Unicorn and returns registers and NZCV, cross-checked
by an independent Python model on 11 edge cases (every flag set at least once).
test_recompile_arith.py lifts `arith` with remill-lift, compiles it with clang++ against
remill_host.cpp and compares x0 and NZCV with the reference. Skipped without REMILL_BUILD or
unicorn. A function needing memory or call intrinsics fails the link: an explicit error.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: T2 of an AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); tests and a host stub only, nothing in the host, loader or shader chain changes
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-recompilation-arm64)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
